sequenceDiagram
    participant User as User / kubectl
    participant K8sAPI as Kubernetes API<br/>6443/TCP HTTPS
    participant Webhook as Validating Webhook<br/>9443/TCP HTTPS
    participant Controller as MCPServer Controller
    participant K8sRes as Kubernetes Resources
    participant MCPServer as Managed MCP Server<br/>spec.config.port/TCP
    participant GWCtrl as Gateway Provider Controller
    participant GW as Gateway / HTTPRoute

    Note over User,GW: Flow 1: MCPServer Lifecycle

    User->>K8sAPI: kubectl apply MCPServer CR<br/>Auth: User credentials
    K8sAPI->>Webhook: POST /validate-mcp-x-k8s-io-v1alpha1-mcpserver<br/>TLS (cert-manager)
    Webhook-->>K8sAPI: Admission Response<br/>(validates image allowlist, digest,<br/>storage limits, labels)
    K8sAPI-->>User: MCPServer created

    K8sAPI->>Controller: Watch event: MCPServer CR<br/>ServiceAccount token
    Controller->>K8sAPI: Create/Update Deployment<br/>TLS 1.2+
    Controller->>K8sAPI: Create/Update Service<br/>TLS 1.2+
    Controller->>K8sAPI: Create/Update NetworkPolicy<br/>TLS 1.2+
    Controller->>K8sAPI: Set condition: Accepted=True

    K8sRes-->>Controller: Deployment ready
    Controller->>K8sAPI: Set condition: Available=True

    Controller->>MCPServer: MCP protocol handshake<br/>(initialize request via go-sdk)<br/>HTTP or HTTPS (configurable)
    MCPServer-->>Controller: Handshake response
    Controller->>K8sAPI: Set condition: Verified=True

    Note over User,GW: Flow 2: Gateway Integration (httproute)

    Controller->>K8sAPI: Create MCPGatewayBinding CR
    K8sAPI->>GWCtrl: Watch event: MCPGatewayBinding<br/>(filtered by provider name)
    GWCtrl->>K8sAPI: Read Gateway resource
    GWCtrl->>K8sAPI: Create HTTPRoute<br/>(parentRef → Gateway,<br/>backendRef → MCP server Service)

    Note over User,GW: External access now active

    User->>GW: Request via Gateway<br/>HTTPS (Gateway TLS)
    GW->>MCPServer: Route to MCP server Service<br/>via HTTPRoute
    MCPServer-->>GW: Response
    GW-->>User: Response
